    {
      "id": "SFPL",
      "code_hash": "545a520200ac12caaaf278abd3397463",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Things to try: untick <em>amount \u2265 0</em> and pick a negative factor; set the\nthreshold below 0; untick it again, ask for <code>doubled IS NOT NULL</code> and\nthink about why it holds even though <code>amount</code> can now be NULL in the\ninput; tick <em>amount \u2264 100</em> and ask for <code>doubled &lt;= 200</code>.</span>\n<h2 id=\"when-a-proof-fails\">When a proof fails</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A promise that doesn't follow is better caught here than by billing. It\nis refused, with what Lean <em>could</em> establish. Here the precondition\nallows <code>amount = 0</code>, so <code>total</code> can be 1:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "492c0f8fe4f89438707f46cb655fe4ce",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><div class=\"language-text codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>VerificationError: could not prove: (_.total &gt; 5) (it is TRUE or FALSE)\nrequires orders: (_.amount &gt;= 0)\nensures (_.total &gt; 5): NOT proved (it is TRUE or FALSE)\n  counterexample: orders(id, customer, amount) = [(0, '', 0)] gives (id, total) = [(0, 1)]\nwarning: may wrap around: ($2 + 1)\nknown about the output:\n  id: any integer or NULL\n  total: an integer \u2265 1\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "d601fd1b6426b04f2f3053b0e28a514f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">\"It is TRUE or FALSE\" is Lean's honest answer: for some allowed inputs\n<code>total &gt; 5</code> holds, for others it doesn't. Lean never guesses. A refusal\ncan also mean the truth is out of reach of the analysis (the end of this\nchapter lists what it tracks), so a \u274c is \"not proved\", not \"false\".</span>\n<h2 id=\"contracts-on-real-data\">Contracts on real data</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">So far the table had no data: the proof is about <em>every</em> possible\n<code>orders</code>. Real tables come from upstream systems you don't control, and\nbinding the function to them adds two things:</span>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Preconditions are checked on the data</strong> at call time, because they\n   are assumptions about the outside world, and the outside world lies.\n   A violation raises <code>PreconditionError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Unproved postconditions</strong> can be checked on the output instead of\n   refusing the call, with <code>on_unproved</code>:</li>\n</ol>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>on_unproved=</code></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">what happens when a postcondition isn't proved</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>\"error\"</code> (default)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">raise <code>VerificationError</code>; nothing runs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>\"runtime\"</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">run the pipeline and check that condition on the actual output; raise <code>PostconditionError</code> on a violation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>\"warn\"</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">issue a warning and carry on</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Some data, with a sneaky NULL:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "0b11448bbe361d6b6086a919a69d92c6",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>orders</strong></span></span><table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;width:auto;margin:0'><thead><tr><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>id</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>customer</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>1</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>ada</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>30</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>bob</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>5</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>3</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>cy</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5'>NULL</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "8b8ec17bf75edfe3ee0aad73bb0808d1",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: row;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 2rem'><marimo-ui-element object-id='emfo-0' random-id='71dfb1c5-1067-e4f9-de3d-d18d93d2a13a'><marimo-radio data-initial-value='&quot;runtime&quot;' data-label='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eon_unproved&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-options='[&quot;error&quot;,&quot;runtime&quot;,&quot;warn&quot;]' data-inline='true' data-disabled='false'></marimo-radio></marimo-ui-element><marimo-ui-element object-id='emfo-1' random-id='e9af41fc-4617-e008-fb0d-1eaff0293d5f'><marimo-switch data-initial-value='false' data-label='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003erequires amount \u2265 0&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-disabled='false'></marimo-switch></marimo-ui-element></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
