    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "03374bfc9a720d09281c21e7c80abe76",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">With the default settings, <code>amount &lt; 100</code> can't be proved (nothing bounds\n<code>amount</code>), so <code>\"runtime\"</code> checks it on the output. It fails for one row,\nand it's <code>cy</code>'s: <strong>NULL &lt; 100 is not TRUE</strong>, so the NULL row counts as a\nviolation. A contract condition must be TRUE, not merely \"not FALSE\".</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Switch on <em>requires amount \u2265 0</em>: now the precondition check fails first,\nfor the same NULL. Pass <code>check_requires=False</code> to <code>sv.transform</code> to trust\nthe inputs instead (the proofs then rest on that trust).</span>\n<h3 id=\"schemas-count-too\">Schemas count too</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A column declared non-nullable (<code>\"!int64\"</code> in Ibis) is never NULL, and\nLean knows it, so <code>amount IS NOT NULL</code> needs no precondition:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "iLit",
      "code_hash": "bf57dc4c40ee35dc0917f5ae678b283d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>postcondition</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>amount IS NOT NULL</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>output column</th>\n<th>known values</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>id</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>amount</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
