    {
      "id": "ZHCJ",
      "code_hash": "fb050a814e98070d53e612f8dc500d08",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"the-theorem-behind-the\">The theorem behind the \u2705</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">When a reviewer asks why they should believe a \u2705, this is the answer.\nEvery \u2705 in this tour is an instance of <code>contract_sound</code> in\n<code>SubstraitLean/Contracts.lean</code>:</span>\n<div class=\"language-lean codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">contract_sound</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cat.WF</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2208</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rows</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EnvMem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">               </span><span class=\"c1\">-- rows match the schema</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hpre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2208</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rows</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2208</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e.eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isTrue</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- preconditions hold</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hQ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q.WF</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hproved</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q.aeval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tableEnv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AVal.certainlyTrue</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2208</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q.eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cat</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2200</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\u2208</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">row</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\">                   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- postconditions hold</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Read: <em>if every input row matches its schema and satisfies the\npreconditions, and the abstract interpretation (<code>aeval</code>) says every\npostcondition is certainly TRUE, then every postcondition is TRUE on\nevery output row.</em> <code>hproved</code> is what the checker computes for your plan;\nthe rest are assumptions about the data, which <code>sverify</code> checks when the\ndata is there.</span>\n<h2 id=\"what-lean-tracks\">What Lean tracks</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Per column: whether it can be NULL, an integer or double range, which\nbooleans it can be, timestamps, and whether it can be a string. Filters\nsuch as <code>amount &gt; 10</code>, <code>x = 3</code>, <code>x IN (1, 2, 3)</code> and <code>x IS NOT NULL</code>\nrefine those facts; arithmetic, comparisons, <code>AND</code>/<code>OR</code>/<code>NOT</code> with SQL's\nNULL semantics, <code>CASE</code>, <code>COALESCE</code>, joins and <code>UNION ALL</code> propagate them.\nThe next chapters add <strong>keys</strong> and <strong>relations between columns</strong> (5),\nruntime errors (6) and window functions (7); doubles, time and text\nhave a chapter of their own (12).</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Not tracked yet: relations that need more than \"column plus constant\"\n(<code>a &lt; 2 * b</code>), string contents, DECIMAL columns, and counts across rows.\nPostconditions like those are refused rather than guessed; use\n<code>on_unproved=\"runtime\"</code> to check them on the data instead.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">You can now put a contract on a transformation, read what Lean proved\nabout every column, and choose what happens when a promise can't be\nproved. The billing job gets a column whose promises were proved\nbefore any data ran, and the assumptions about upstream data are\nchecked when the data arrives. <strong>Next up:</strong>\n<a href=\"?file=05_keys_and_relations.py\">Keys and relations</a>, where the facts\nare about pairs of rows and pairs of columns.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
